Spec: SpecDD Path Reference Extractor

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Extract path and glob candidates from SpecDD text.

Owns:
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt

Can modify:
  SpecDDPathReferenceExtractor.kt

Can read:
  ../parser/*
  ../../../../../../test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/references/SpecDDPathReferenceExtractorBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Use `SpecDDLineClassifier` to identify sections and body line shapes.
  Track the current known section while scanning lines.
  Extract bare key text before `:` from key-value lines only inside `Structure`, `Owns`, `Can modify`, `Can read`, `References`, `Depends on`, `Forbids`, and `Exposes`.
  Treat bare key candidates from path-bearing sections as path candidates even when they do not contain explicit path syntax.
  Extract inline path-like candidates from task lines, scenario steps, key-value lines, and ordinary body text.
  Recognize inline candidates with relative path prefixes, slash-separated path segments, glob characters, or known source, spec, data, and markup file extensions.
  Ignore blank lines, comments, section headers, and non-path prose.
  Preserve exact candidate text ranges in file coordinates.
  Mark candidates with path syntax when they contain `/`, `.`, `*`, `?`, `[`, `]`, `{`, `}`, or start with `~`.

Must not:
  Resolve paths.
  Create IntelliJ PSI references.
  Report diagnostics.
